1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:00,620
Hi.

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:04,850
Okay, Finally, it's time to talk about CV.

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:06,920
Why do you need it?

4
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:11,450
What should you include and not include in your CV?

5
00:00:11,930 --> 00:00:13,010
Let's go.

6
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:22,940
CV or resume is the short document with the most important information about your professional experience

7
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:30,230
skills achievements that show that you are the right person for the job you are applying for.

8
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:33,260
And this is an example of a CV.

9
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:35,780
Okay.

10
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:37,890
Why do we need a CV?

11
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:39,060
What is a CV?

12
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:49,710
Goal To show that your skills and experience fit the job requirements and to get you an invitation to

13
00:00:49,710 --> 00:00:50,850
the interview.

14
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:52,440
All right.

15
00:00:53,190 --> 00:00:55,800
What should you include in your CV?

16
00:00:56,550 --> 00:00:58,050
Your name, of course.

17
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:05,520
Contact details, summary of your skills and experience skills, both hard and soft.

18
00:01:05,550 --> 00:01:07,620
Your working Experience.

19
00:01:07,770 --> 00:01:14,970
Education certificates and some personal information about your interests and hobbies.

20
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:24,810
What not to include your age, marital status, religion, gender, sexual orientation or political

21
00:01:24,810 --> 00:01:25,640
preferences.

22
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:31,860
It's not professional to include those things in your CV structure.

23
00:01:31,890 --> 00:01:40,950
Start with your name, your position, give contact information, summary or your career goal.

24
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,190
Your skills.

25
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:50,380
Then list your work, experience education, add some trainings or certificates that are relevant to

26
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:55,120
the job, and at the end you can add some personal interests.

27
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:56,660
Okay.

28
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,210
Contact information.

29
00:01:58,210 --> 00:02:07,240
Include your email, your phone number, your location, your links to LinkedIn, GitHub, link or portfolio.

30
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:09,980
But don't write your full address.

31
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,680
It's not necessary.

32
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,880
Professional Summary.

33
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:23,080
So have a look at these two examples of summaries and decide what is the role, the position of these

34
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:23,860
people.

35
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:25,840
Yeah, that's right.

36
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:33,170
This is an engineer and this is a back end developer specializing in Python.

37
00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:38,830
Okay, so when you write a summary, write how many years of experience you have?

38
00:02:38,830 --> 00:02:44,860
What are your major skills and maybe some major achievement?

39
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:48,190
Skills, okay.

40
00:02:48,190 --> 00:02:54,160
Include both hard and soft skills as well as language knowledge.

41
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:54,870
Okay.

42
00:02:54,880 --> 00:03:05,290
As you can see from those skills, this is a CV of a QA engineer and here is a CV of probably project

43
00:03:05,290 --> 00:03:06,250
manager.

44
00:03:08,370 --> 00:03:10,440
Work experience.

45
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:19,470
When you describe your work experience, start with your most recent job, so use reverse chronology

46
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:21,660
for listing your jobs.

47
00:03:21,810 --> 00:03:24,420
Describe your position.

48
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:29,200
Give the name of your company and how long you work there.

49
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:32,820
If you are still working at that company, write.

50
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:42,010
From the start till present or now, and use numbers to show your achievements.

51
00:03:42,010 --> 00:03:50,950
For example, maintained 250 windows computers saved four hours a week.

52
00:03:51,610 --> 00:03:52,390
Good.

53
00:03:53,320 --> 00:04:02,830
Also mention your education and write about your certificates or training related to this position.

54
00:04:05,730 --> 00:04:08,250
Hobbies and interests.

55
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:09,030
Okay.

56
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:13,140
Don't write something like reading traveling music.

57
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:14,920
It's too general.

58
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:16,780
Everyone does that.

59
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:26,010
Instead, you can say I was a member of a music band, or I read all the books by George Martin or visited

60
00:04:26,010 --> 00:04:28,620
ten countries in one year.

61
00:04:28,650 --> 00:04:32,010
Be specific and try to be interesting.

62
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:33,480
Okay.

63
00:04:33,510 --> 00:04:34,830
More tips.

64
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:38,820
Choose an appropriate name for the file.

65
00:04:39,690 --> 00:04:42,150
Copy Free CV for free.

66
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:45,660
Free is not a good way to name your file.

67
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:49,950
Instead, write your name and position.

68
00:04:49,950 --> 00:04:52,980
Kate Johnson, Project Manager.

69
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:58,530
With this name, your CV will be more visible to recruiters.

70
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,360
Okay.

71
00:04:59,370 --> 00:05:03,030
Don't write the desired salary in your CV.

72
00:05:03,210 --> 00:05:09,730
If your email address sounds like hot boy at gmail.com, change it.

73
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:14,560
You don't look professional with email like that.

74
00:05:14,830 --> 00:05:21,970
Don't write about your driving license because it's not necessary if you are applying for it.

75
00:05:21,970 --> 00:05:22,570
Job.

76
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:32,440
Remove references available upon request because it's obvious it's not necessary to have this sentence

77
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:40,930
in your CV and if you decide to include your photo, include only professional picture, something like

78
00:05:40,930 --> 00:05:42,670
your LinkedIn picture.

79
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:45,730
All right, thank you.

80
00:05:45,730 --> 00:05:50,590
And more CV examples and practice in your file by.
